#lang saffron
;; saffron-lang-plan D5: the Saffron -> Turmeric seam CHECKS rather than erases.
;;
;; `takes-int` has a real signature and the caller hands it an `any` holding a
;; cstr.  D5 rejected erasure explicitly: passing the payload word through
;; unchecked would turn this type error into a memory-safety bug, because the
;; word is a `const char *` being read as an int.  The seam reuses the checked
;; unbox `(cast x T)` lowers to, so the failure is a panic naming the mismatch.
;;
;; requires.interp-only: the compiled back end reports the S5 gap for the
;; dynamic operators in this program before it could reach the seam.
(defn takes-int [n : int] : int (+ n 1))
(defn dyn [v] v)
(defn main [] : int
  (println (takes-int (dyn "not an int")))
  0)
